mantle rm199
state ready
dialect plain
accent broad light
tier full
written_for rm_clemence_rustham
title the last warm saucer
fits stage=adult|old
prefers role=merchant job=cook
traits temper=calm talk=plain warmth=reserved humour=none honesty=plain piety=ordinary drive=steady
quirk chalks_a_coal_ring_under_the_last_saucer
likes crisp_apples riddles quiet_chapel autumn_wind
dislikes early_bells rats
fears a_place_that_cools_unnoticed
hopes a_bowl_for_the_late_arrival
topics food +0.7 newcomer +0.5 work +0.4 pastimes +0.2 gossip -0.4
styles comfort=food gossip=reserved refuse=gentle tease=none
marks oath saying
persona #self.first# keeps a coal nub for marking the last warm saucer and receives strangers with quiet, unhurried pride.

words
oath! = Blacken the trivet | By my last blue saucer
saying! = Welcome fits a shallow dish | The last bowl is a promise
coal = my lucky coal nub | the bit of black in my pocket
ring = a broken circle | my mark underneath
saucer = a blue saucer | the thin blue dish
spoon = a polished horn spoon | the blunt little dipper
hearth = the warm lip of the hearth | the edge of the firebed
skin = a long narrow apple shaving | a curly strip of peel
steam = a veil off the pot | that breath above the broth
apple = an apple that snaps | a firm sharp apple
napkin = a square of soft linen | the folded cloth
thumbmark = the black print of my thumb | a sooty whorl
riddle = a puzzle for after supper | a small knot of a question
wait = time enough for two long breaths | a decent interval
clove = a dry clove bud | the clove with the crooked stem
cover = a snug little lid | the saucer upside down
bench = the seat nearest the heat | the inner stool
scrap = the little heel of onion | an end of sweet root

any
opinion city for 2 : Whatever hour your fire goes out, there's another bright window in the city.
opinion merchants for 1 : A decent trader counts the ones who leave empty as well as the ones who pay.
opinion road against 1 : A rut asks the same toll of a barrow carrying supper as a coach carrying velvet.
opinion watch for 1 : When two angry customers want the same place, I appreciate a quiet uniform nearby.
opinion dole for 1 : Some hunger can wait for an answer. A hungry pup can't.
opinion church mixed 1 : My thoughts carry better under a chapel roof. The sermons vary.
opinion festivals mixed 1 : I like the part where everyone sits to eat and nobody has to carry a banner.
opinion newcomers for 2 : A stranger knows the trick I missed because I've done a thing the same way all my life.
opinion drink mixed 1 : Wine in a stew has all evening to improve its manners.

grown
line greet : Pull a little space towards you. There's enough warmth to go round. | Come through. Crowding won't spoil the welcome.
line greet [pair.band=strangers] : A first visit gets the comfortable seat. | Settle before you say what brought you.
line greet [here.time=dawn] : There's a good clean light on everything yet. | There's the first light. Bring yourself in with it.
line greet [here.time=dusk|night] : Come clear of the dark first. I can see you now. | I have a welcome left even at this hour.
line greet.return : Yes, I'm quite at liberty to listen. | Hello there. You've caught a quiet moment.
line greet.return [pair.band=friends|family] : Your familiar face warms up the whole place. | Ah, the very face I was saving a smile for.
line again.open : There's a second helping of your company today. | Plenty of day for us to meet twice in it.
line kin.open [pair.kin!=no] : Come take the close seat. A relation fits in the small gap. | I'd squeeze in a relation even if only the narrow stool were left.
line hail [pair.band=friends] : This way. I've room for the whole of you. | A friendly face at that distance ought to be nearer.
line farewell : Carry a little warmth along with you. | Go when it suits you. Nobody's counting mouthfuls.
line farewell.return : May supper meet you halfway home. | A kind evening where your road ends.
line react.news : Start with what happened. We can decide how it tastes afterwards. | Let me get the plain account before anyone spices it.
line react.news.new : I haven't served that piece of news before. | Fresh to my ears. I'll let it settle.
line react.news.known : Yes, that one's cooled a little since first hearing. | That news and I have already sat together once.
line react.news.doubt : I'd leave that covered till a witness comes in. | A bold tale needs something solid underneath.
line react.news.sorrow [topic.kind=death|loss|theft|assault|arrest|crime] : I'll make room for whoever needs to sit with it. | May nobody have to go back to an empty room after that.
line react.news.glad [topic.kind=birth|work|marriage|succession|apprentice] : That's news I'd lay the good cloth out for. | That leaves a lovely taste long after the words have gone.
line ask.how : Have you had an hour to call your own yet? | Has this day fed you or eaten you up?
line answer.how : I can stand my own company today. That usually does it. | As patient as I need to be, which is a blessing.
line answer.how.busy [self.working=yes] : There's an order to this rush. I'm still on top of it. | I've near enough fingers for everything that needs attending.
line sympathise : You're entitled to be tired before you start explaining. | There's no charge for sitting without a single word to say.
line reassure : One thing you can lay down already. I'll remember that bit. | A slow breath comes first. Explanations can have the second.
line decline : Leave me out, please. Somebody may still need my place. | I'd best stay within earshot a little longer.
line accept_decline : Then we'll take the spare setting back. | I can take no for a courteous answer.
line thank : You noticed without my having to ask. Much appreciated. | You made something easier without making a show of it. Thank you.
line deflect_thanks : Nothing was spoilt by sharing it. | It's a poor kindness that expects to be repaid at once.
line preclose : I'll gather my thoughts before they boil right over. | Seems I've another place to be before I forget it.
line accept_preclose : Take a good breath before you stand. | Let's get you on your feet by degrees.
line check_in : Comfortable where you are, or shall we make a little space? | Anything you can't get at from that seat?
line give.advice : Do the waiting part before you call somebody over. | Don't keep a guest watching while you try to hurry what can't hurry.
line ack : I'm quite with you. | That part's clear enough.

scene lastdish
when topic=work self.job=cook
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : See the dark arc under #saucer#? | I turn one dish upside down before service.
b : Doesn't the scullery scrub it off? | Is that dish chipped?
a : Every time. I put it back myself. That's how I remember the last portion. | It's keeping the place for whoever comes too late.


scene latewolves
when topic=newcomer self.job=cook
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : A late arrival looks at the benches before the menu. | I offer the last bowl without asking where a stranger's been.
b : Afraid of missing dinner? | You must wonder.
a : More afraid of being the reason somebody has to get up. | Of course. Curiosity can wait through supper.


scene appletest
when topic=food self.likes=crisp_apples
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I listen for the snap when I cut #apple#. | I leave the best side of an apple till last.
b : You judge with your ears? | How do you pick the best side?
a : A clean snap means eat it raw. A sigh means stew it gently. | Take two bites. You'll find your jaw has decided already.


scene blackthumb
when topic=smalltalk
does tell.complaint / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I put #thumbmark# on my nose again. | I've a perfect whorl in black on this linen.
b : Want a cloth? | How do you know whose?
a : Yes, but hand it to my clean side or we'll be here all night. | It matches the gap where my pocket coal rubs my thumb bare.


scene riddle
when topic=pastimes self.likes=riddles
does ask.detail / answer.detail / assess
a : I vanish in a ladle and reappear in six bowls. Guess. | When does a cook prefer a poor memory?
b : A promise of dinner? | When the soup burns?
a : That's better than my answer. My answer was a pinch of pepper. | Exactly. Particularly in the customers.


scene chapel
when topic=faith self.likes=quiet_chapel
does tell.feeling / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : When the last hymn stops I like to stay in my seat. | I like a chapel where the door shuts softly.
b : Waiting for another? | Why the door particularly?
a : Waiting to hear what else is in the room besides us. | You can take your place without everybody turning to measure your faith.


scene wind
when topic=season here.season=autumn
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : Autumn lifts the leaves like lids off little invisible pots. | I've a taste for autumn wind after a close room.
b : You see a kitchen everywhere. | You look quite pink about it.
a : The whole city has an appetite. I reckon I'm in good company. | Good. I was afraid I'd come out looking boiled.


scene bells
when topic=day here.time=dawn self.dislikes=early_bells
does tell.complaint / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I'd like a bell to wake up as gradually as a kettle. | The first bell takes up all the room in my head.
b : Start with a murmur? | What does the second do?
a : Yes. Give a sleeping wolf one breath to decide to be civil. | Finds me awake enough to object.


scene rats
when topic=animals self.dislikes=rats
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I don't mind a clever beast until it gets ideas about supper. | I'd make a dreadful rat.
b : What kind of ideas? | Too big for the hole?
a : Private dining in my oatmeal bin, chiefly. | Too proud to eat what's been dropped. I'd want a plate.


scene potquiet
when topic=work self.job=cook
does give.advice / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : If you have to shout over a simmer you've turned it up too high. | Tip the lid and wait for #steam# to choose a side.
b : Even with dried peas? | Then lift from the other?
a : Especially peas. They'll turn your nice lid into a drum. | Precisely. Keep your face for something better than testing soup.


scene roads
when topic=caravan world.wagons=late
does tell.worry / react.self / assess
a : A late wagon gives you two suppers to think about. | Late wagons are easier on a pantry than on a promise.
b : The one you planned and the one you'll manage? | Does a promise run out sooner?
a : Exactly. And never tell a hungry table the first one. | It starts running the moment you give it.


scene debt
when topic=prices self.owes=yes
does tell.worry / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : My debt's got a place at table ahead of me. | I don't call borrowed money an ingredient.
b : Do you feed it first? | Why would anyone?
a : A little each time. I shan't let it take the entire dish. | Some reckon a meal made cheap when someone else paid for the fire.


scene hardtimes
when topic=times world.times=hard|lean
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : When things grow lean, a thin onion sliced thin goes further still. | There's a shame about asking for the heel when times turn.
b : It doesn't grow any bigger. | Could you offer it first?
a : No. But every spoon gets a strip of it. | That's my practice. I say I'd be grateful for help finishing it.


scene door
when topic=home
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I like a door to swing both ways when my paws are full. | A proper hook for a cloth is just high enough to keep the ends clean.
b : Don't you get hit coming through? | How do you measure?
a : Once. After that you announce your elbows. | Hang the longest cloth, then lift the hook a little if you must.


scene table
when topic=friends
does tell.feeling / react.self / assess
a : I like the company that can sit through the scraping of plates. | A long table gives a shy guest two possible neighbours.
b : It's a dismal noise. | Might they both talk?
a : Yes. It means everybody ate. | Perhaps. Then there's company without the burden of starting it.


scene coalstory
when topic=lore
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : #coal.capitalize# has a worn white stripe. | I carry a coal nub past all the handsome stones on the road.
b : Through the black? | Even a smooth piece of quartz?
a : Just on one side, where I've polished it against a seam. | Quartz can't mark a place for someone. Mine earns its keep.


scene bread
when topic=food
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : For a crusty top I leave a little space where the lid sits. | If the crust cracks before the knife touches it, somebody's been patient.
b : Won't the heat escape? | And if the middle's raw?
a : A little. It's the damp I'm showing out. | Somebody's been patient outside the wrong oven.


scene counter
when topic=prices self.role=merchant
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I give a buyer one number and let the face answer. | Counting coin across food makes me twitch.
b : What if the answer's a frown? | In case it falls in?
a : Then I ask what size would suit the purse. | Worse to think of where it's been before it falls.


scene hours
when topic=day
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I mark an hour by the number of times my tea has been warmed. | Three scraps of quiet make me a good long hour.
b : Does it keep accurate time? | By adding them?
a : It keeps an excellent account of interruptions. | By doing the same pleasure in all three and keeping my place.


scene mending
when topic=pastimes
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : A clean darn around a scorch can make it look intended. | My sewing's too tight when I'm cross.
b : Like a flower? | Can you tell afterward?
a : Like a ring where a flower might have been. I'm no embroiderer. | I can date my quarrels by the puckers in a hem.


scene goodbatch
when topic=work self.job=cook
does tell.feeling / react.self / assess
a : My best seasoning today was leaving the pot alone. | A meal with just enough salt makes everybody thirsty later.
b : Hard to leave well enough? | Isn't that too much?
a : Hard when one's paid to look busy. | No. Too much makes them thirsty before the second spoon.


scene gossip
when topic=gossip here.gossip=yes
does tell.gossip / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : The talk is that #topic.subject# #topic.claim#. | I've heard it said that #topic.subject# #topic.claim#.
b : How much of that will you repeat? | Is that your own account?
a : That much. I wasn't given a second helping. | No. It came to me in words and that's how it leaves.


scene friend
when topic=friends self.friend
does tell.feeling / react.self / assess
a : I'd trust #self.friend# with the quiet end of an afternoon. | For #self.friend# I'd keep #bench# by the fire.
b : Does quiet take trust? | That's a comfortable compliment.
a : Quite a lot if you mean to keep it. | The kind I'd choose to receive myself.


scene injury
when topic=health
does give.advice / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : Use a dry cloth to pick up anything hot. | When your feet ache, sit before setting the chair exactly straight.
b : Why especially dry? | I could have thought of that.
a : Steam goes through a wet cloth faster than a shout travels. | So could I. You'd think I'd do it sooner.


scene feast
when topic=festival
does tell.plan / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I'd like the best of the feast served to whoever washes up. | Set a place for the music once the tunes run out.
b : Before or after? | All the musicians?
a : Before. No feast survives the washing in decent shape. | Yes. They need room for their elbows without their instruments, too.


scene distant
when topic=travel
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : I find the first meal in a strange place worth remembering. | I don't ask a carter how far till I've asked where supper lies.
b : The food tells you where you've arrived? | You'd travel by the plate?
a : The asking tells me how long I want to stay. | By the welcome. A cold plate in kind company counts too.


scene weather
when topic=weather here.weather=rain
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : Rain on a lid sounds remarkably like impatient claws. | I'm fond of the little streams this rain runs down the glass.
b : Did you think you had company? | You don't mind the view going?
a : I opened up twice. After that I left the rain to entertain itself. | It brings the window closer. I notice the woodwork.


scene empty
when topic=dreams
does tell.plan / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I'd like one evening when nothing's waiting for another five minutes. | I've a dream of a cupboard with a single bowl in it.
b : What would fill your evening? | Only one?
a : Taste the first mouthful at exactly the right moment. | Just one with a chip. All the good ones are out being used.


scene fire
when topic=work self.job=cook
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : A dying fire'll sometimes cook an egg better than a fierce one. | I move a hot pot by the tune it sings.
b : Is there a trick to it? | Are you listening to the lid?
a : Knowing exactly when the egg wants no more attention. | To the base. A dry patch hisses sharper than the rest.


scene seat
when topic=smalltalk
does offer / react.self / assess
a : Try #bench# before you decide on a better seat. | If a seat wobbles, turn it first.
b : That's quite a short seat. | Why not wedge the foot?
a : A short one lets your heels rest while you eat. | Might be the floor that's tired. Try it two boards over.


story saucerfray [topic=memories]
  : I once laid a blue saucer on a frayed white cuff without looking. Thought I'd chipped the edge.
  : Turned it round and the chip stayed exactly where it was.
  b : Your cuff was the one that needed mending?
  : Yes. I had corrected my table manners at the expense of my sleeve.


story turnip [topic=food]
  : I scooped a little turnip out to make a cup for pepper.
  : A hungry guest took the whole thing in one bite.
  ask : Could you have kept a straight face?
  b : I'd have passed the water first.
  : I did. Only then did I permit myself a very small smile.


story widebench [topic=memories self.age>=25]
  : At a fair I once bought a stool so wide I couldn't reach its ends.
  : By the time I'd turned to pay, a pair of tired travellers had settled on it.
  b : Did you claim your seat?
  : No. I booked my passage on my own stool for when they'd finished their rest.


story halfmeal [topic=work self.job=cook]
  : I once tried to divide a beautiful small pie into seven portions.
  : I spent so long measuring that it cooled and came out of its crust quite whole.
  b : Did you still make seven slices?
  : Seven spoons. The crust was my share.


story littlecoal [topic=lore]
  : An old pot with a pinhole once let a tiny bead of gravy harden on my hearth.
  : I kept it for luck a day. It melted into somebody's apron.
  b : So luck needs a sounder case?
  : That's when I took to carrying the coal. An equally good reminder and it minds the laundry better.


rule @ring
when concept=bark working=yes self.job=cook
does aside
cooldown 8h
say One last blue dish warming. There's time yet for somebody. | Keep the rim hot for the one who'll turn up just after we clear.


rule @slice
when concept=bark working=yes self.job=cook
does aside
cooldown 8h
say Cut the apple across. Fine little star in the heart of it. | Seeds lie crosswise like a little flower in that half. Pass it over.


rule @late
when concept=bark world.wagons=late
does aside
cooldown 8h
say Late goods, long thoughts. What'll stretch till the carts arrive? | If the wagons mean to take all day, the onions can have their time too.


rule @crumb
when concept=bark self.dislikes=rats
does aside
cooldown 8h
say Sweep the corners twice. Whiskers attend to what the broom overlooks. | There's a sharp little nose that knows every crumb I've missed.


rule @season
when concept=bark here.season=autumn
does aside
cooldown 8h
say What a lovely rustle on the step. Autumn's spreading out the cloth. | Crisp underfoot. I'll have leaves in my cuffs by supper.


rule @sole
when concept=bark here.time=dusk|night
does aside
cooldown 8h
say Feet up for just a moment. Even a hearth brick gets to lie down. | A chair at dusk is almost a second pair of shoes.

dlg resident.hub : Rest your paws. I'll listen once you've found a comfortable spot.
dlg resident.hub [topic.meeting=known] : #topic.player#, there's room at this side again.
dlg resident.hub [here.time=night] : On a late visit like this a low voice carries plenty.
dlg resident.hub [pair.disposition=wary|hostile] : If you're after an argument, let everybody else get seated first.
dlg resident.job [self.job=cook] : At #self.workplace# my favourite order is for something a traveller hasn't eaten since coming away.
dlg resident.job : I try to leave enough over for a latecomer.
dlg resident.news [world.news] : What reached my ears was this. #world.news#. Take a moment with it.
dlg resident.gossip [here.gossip=yes] : I hear that #topic.subject# #topic.claim#. I add nothing of my own to a tale already seasoned.
dlg resident.bye : Take the warmth you came in for. Leave the dish here.
dlg shop.greet [here.shop=open] : Come find what your appetite meant when it sent you.
dlg shop.greet [here.shop=bare] : Nothing to go out today. I'll hear what you've brought in.
dlg shop.prices : Name the sum you've set aside and we'll start from that end.
dlg shop.bye [here.shop!=asleep] : May what you carry be just the thing when you get there.
dlg resident.business [business=steady] : Enough to keep the lids in motion. I'm content with that.

graft resident.hub
choice What do you mark with that bit of coal? -> black_saucer
node black_saucer
say A small open circle under a saucer. The missing piece stands for someone who hasn't come in yet.
free
choice Why bother to rub it off? -> black_saucer_more
choice Goodbye. -> bye
node black_saucer_more
say So the next circle has to be made on purpose. An old mark won't remind me half so well.
choice I'll look for the open part. -> hub
choice Goodbye. -> bye


graft shop.greet
choice Where should I set this down while I talk? [here.shop=open] -> warm_corner
node warm_corner
say By the warm corner. The draught misses it and your purchase can wait there till we're done.
free
choice Do you keep a corner for everything? -> warm_corner_more
choice Goodbye. -> bye
node warm_corner_more
say Just one for things that ought to wait. Saves setting them somewhere they oughtn't.
choice I'll leave it there. -> greet
choice Goodbye. -> bye
